-- title:
--   Index of xgΛ̂∩ H as product of local indices
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and write $H=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ for the associated quaternion algebra. Let $\Lambda\subseteq H$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule satisfying `IsOrder`, that is: $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $H$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated. Let $x,g$ be units of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ (the tensor product with the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$), and assume the underlying element of $g$ lies in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral. For a unit $y$, [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\,y$ denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $z\in H$ whose image $z\otimes 1$ lies in $y\cdot$`finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda$. Then the relative index of the additive subgroup of `ofFiniteIdele` $\Lambda\,(xg)$ in that of `ofFiniteIdele` $\Lambda\,x$ equals the finite product, over the places $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathbb{Z}$, of the relative index of the image of [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\,v$ under left multiplication by the $v$-component of $g$ inside `localBox` $\Lambda\,v$; here `localBox` $\Lambda\,v$ is the additive subgroup of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$, $c$ integral, and the $v$-component is taken via the algebra map [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36).
--
--   This is the local–global computation of the index of the right $\Lambda$-lattice $xg\hat\Lambda\cap H$ inside $x\hat\Lambda\cap H$: the index equals $\prod_v[\Lambda_v:g_v\Lambda_v]$ and in particular does not depend on $x$. It is used in the identification of sublattices of a given type with primitive right sublattices of prescribed index, which feeds the description of the double-coset class set for orders in a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_relIndex_ofFiniteIdele_mul_eq_finprod_relIndex_map_mulLeft_localBox.lean

